k><name>FUJIKAKE MASATO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HAMAMOTO SHIGEKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KAWAKITA TOMOKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YOSHINAKA MASATOYO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUJIKAKE, MASATO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HAMAMOTO, SHIGEKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAWAKITA, TOMOKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOSHINAKA, MASATOYO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A carboxylated polymer composition which comprises (A) 100 parts by weight of a carboxylated polymer obtained by copolymerizing (a) an  alpha ,  beta -unsaturated carboxylic acid with (b) a compound having at least two ethylenically unsaturated groups and (B) 0.01 to 20 parts by weight of at least one of (c) a polyhydric alcohol/fatty acid ester and (d) an alkylene oxide adduct of a polyhydric alcohol/fatty acid ester. The composition has excellent solubility in water and is highly effective in thickening aqueous solutions. It is hence suitable for use as a thickener for various aqueous solutions.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Cette composition polymère carboxylée comprend (A) 100 parts en poids d'un polymère carboxylé obtenu par copolymérisation (a) d'un acide carboxylique  alpha ,  beta  insaturé, avec (b) un composé possédant au moins deux groupes à insaturation éthylénique et (B) 0,01 à 20 parts en poids d'au moins (c) un ester d'alcool polyhydrique/d'acide gras et (d) d'un adduit d'oxyde d'alkylène d'un ester d'alcool polyhydrique/d'acide gras. Cette composition possède une excellente solubilité dans l'eau et elle est très efficace pour épaissir des solutions aqueuses. Par conséquent, elle est utile en tant qu'épaississant dans diverses solutions aqueuses.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>